.TH PYCDLIB-DIFF 1 "Nov 2026" "pycdlib-diff"

.SH NAME
pycdlib-diff \- tool to compare two ISO images by content and identity

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pycdlib-diff [OPTIONS] \-\-new <iso-file> [\-\-old <iso-file>]

.SH DESCRIPTION
pycdlib-diff compares two ISO images without assuming that either image kept
its original on-disk layout.  It walks one namespace (Rock Ridge, UDF, Joliet,
or ISO9660), hashes every file, and matches entries between the images using
path evidence and content digests together.  Extents, path tables, and block
ordering are not used to decide identity, so re-mastered images with identical
content produce an empty report.

The report keeps three kinds of logical change separate:

.IP "content updates"
An entry with the same identity whose data digest changed.
.IP "path migrations"
An entry whose data digest is unchanged but whose path moved.
.IP "attribute-only changes"
An entry whose data and path are unchanged but whose directory-record
attributes (mode, ownership, link count, and optionally timestamps) changed.

It additionally reports changes in which files share data blocks, since a
re-master can split or create hard links without changing any file content.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-old " <iso-file>"
The old image.  When omitted, the new image is still inspected, but the report
does not infer that any entry was removed, because without a complete old
image there is nothing to compare against.
.TP
.BI \-\-new " <iso-file>"
The new image.  Required.
.TP
.BI \-\-namespace " [auto,rr,udf,joliet,iso]"
The namespace to compare.  The default, auto, prefers Rock Ridge, then UDF,
then Joliet, then ISO9660, using the first namespace both images provide.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " [text,json]"
The report format.  The default is text.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " <file>"
Write the report to this file instead of standard output.
.TP
.B \-\-fail\-on\-diff
Exit with status 1 when at least one content update, path migration,
attribute-only change, shared-block change, addition, or removal is found.
Ambiguous or unverified entries alone do not set this status.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The images were compared successfully (with or without differences).
.TP
.B 1
A difference was found and \-\-fail\-on\-diff was supplied.
.TP
.B 2
An ISO could not be opened or the arguments were invalid.

.SH IDENTITY RULES
A same-path pair of entries with different digests is a content update: the
path proves they are the same entry, and the digest proves the data changed.
A pair at different paths with the same digest is a path migration.  A
directory whose complete subtree signature is unchanged can be matched even
when it was renamed, and a directory whose relative names and kinds are
unchanged provides the evidence to pair a moved file whose contents were also
rewritten.  When several entries share a digest and the directory evidence
cannot choose between them, the report lists the entry as ambiguous rather
than guessing.

If the old image is missing, truncated, or otherwise incomplete, entries that
are unmatched are reported as unverified and are never reported as removed.

.SH SEE ALSO
pycdlib-explorer(1), pycdlib-extract-files(1), pycdlib-genisoimage(1)

